 "traps": [
  "Android units use Jetpack Compose (androidx.compose BOM) while :common, :compose-desktop and :compose-web use JetBrains Compose Multiplatform: two names for related frameworks, attributed per unit",
  ":wearApp adds Compose for Wear OS and Horologist; Glance, Wear Tiles and ProtoLayout are Jetpack libraries not counted as frameworks here",
  "the SwiftUI app (an Xcode target) and the WinUI app (windows/WinUiApp, a .NET project consuming the Kotlin library as the NuGet package PeopleInSpace.Kotlin) are outside Gradle",
  "kotlin.test, the Kotlin test framework, appears only as kotlin(\"test\") in commonTest and jvmTest; Robolectric only in the Android unit tests",
  "webpack is driven by the Kotlin/Wasm Gradle plugin: there is no package.json, only devNpm declarations and webpack.config.d/",
  "every external service is an HTTP API named by a base URL in code (wheretheiss.at, astroviewer.net, thespacedevs.com) or a map SDK; the backend is deployed to Google App Engine by backend/src/jvmMain/appengine/app.yaml",
  "only frameworks and services are measured; the other facets are in unknown"
 ],
